From 1f8a5020afc8913384151f4a32f06edc91c2e6c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:00:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sidebar): a cold session with history never reads as a
 draft [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A settled session nothing shows has its transcript released (messages: []).
$draftSessionIds called any empty client state a draft unless its row was in
$sessions with message_count > 0, but project-tree rows older than the recents
page are not in $sessions. Such a chat (207 messages) painted the "Draft —
nothing sent yet" dot and no stripe, instead of green done, until a reload
dropped the client state.

- releaseSessionTranscript marks the state transcriptReleased; $draftSessionIds
  never counts a released state as unsent.
- withRowActivity: the row's own message_count > 0 beats a store draft claim.

Tests: session-dot-state.test.ts (released state with no listed row, row with
messages vs a draft claim, controls for a real unsent tab / message_count 0).
